### Filmjury API Tests (HTTP Client)
### Compatible with IntelliJ IDEA HTTP Client, VS Code REST Client, and similar tools.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### =========================================================================
### 1. Criteria Endpoints (/api/criteria)
### =========================================================================

### 1.1 Get All Criteria
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/criteria
Accept: application/json

###

### 1.2 Create Criterion
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/criteria
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Cinematography",
  "description": "Visual aesthetics, composition, lighting, and camera movement",
  "maxScore": 20
}

###

### 1.3 Create Another Criterion (Directing)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/criteria
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Direction & Storytelling",
  "description": "Pacing, dramatic structure, and overall narrative vision",
  "maxScore": 25
}

###

### 1.4 Update Criterion (PUT)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/criteria/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Cinematography & Visual Design",
  "description": "Visual aesthetics, composition, lighting, camera angles, and color palette",
  "maxScore": 20
}

###

### 1.5 Delete Criterion (DELETE - returns 204 if deleted, 404 if not found)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/criteria/999
Accept: application/json

###

### =========================================================================
### 2. Judges Endpoints (/api/judges)
### =========================================================================

### 2.1 Get All Judges
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/judges
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.2 Create Judge
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/judges
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Christopher Nolan",
  "contactDetails": "nolan@syncopyfilms.com"
}

###

### 2.3 Create Another Judge
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/judges
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Greta Gerwig",
  "contactDetails": "greta@filmmakers.org"
}

###

### =========================================================================
### 3. Entries Endpoints (/api/entries)
### =========================================================================

### 3.1 Get All Entries
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/entries
Accept: application/json

###

### 3.2 Create Entry (Film Submission)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Echoes of Time",
  "genre": "Sci-Fi / Drama",
  "videoLink": "https://vimeo.com/sample-echoes-of-time",
  "teamDetails": "Director: Vignesh R, Cinematographer: Alex Morgan, Editor: Sarah Connor"
}

###

### 3.3 Create Another Entry
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "The Silent Horizon",
  "genre": "Documentary",
  "videoLink": "https://vimeo.com/sample-silent-horizon",
  "teamDetails": "Director: Jane Doe, Producer: Arctic Media Group"
}

###

### 3.4 Get Leaderboard (Sorted by finalScore descending)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/entries/leaderboard
Accept: application/json

###

### =========================================================================
### 4. Contest Workflow Endpoints (/api/contest)
### =========================================================================

### 4.1 Assign Judge to Entry
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contest/assign-judge?entryId=1&judgeId=1
Accept: text/plain

###

### 4.2 Submit Scorecard for Entry
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contest/submit-score
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entry": {
    "id": 1
  },
  "judge": {
    "id": 1
  },
  "criteriaScores": {
    "1": 18,
    "2": 23
  }
}

###

### =========================================================================
### 5. OpenAPI & Swagger UI Documentation Endpoints
### =========================================================================

### 5.1 OpenAPI Specification (v3/api-docs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v3/api-docs
Accept: application/json

###

### 5.2 Swagger UI HTML
GET {{baseUrl}}/swagger-ui.html
